 "text": "Hi, how have you been? A sketch is usually shorter than a study, often only one or two minutes long, and it usually shows one character or small interaction. A study, on the other hand, lasts several minutes to a few minutes. Not exactly. A study is more like a performance, it' supposed to show a character in detail, and it' often drawn from life. Then think you should start each sketch with a clear title. Say something like, A cloudy morning, or Clouds casting shadows on the upper field. People know what they' getting and it helps them pick the right one. Show the main subject of each one, with the name written below if necessary. People skim through drawings so a clear title is useful. Clouds looking menacing. Clouds casting shadows. Clouds playing hide and seek. Those all work? Clouds looking menacing is my favorite. You' welcome.",
